    description: "Invariant: the websocket linker detects the Django Channels send idiom used inside sync consumers.\n\nViolated today: `DJANGO_ASYNC_SEND` (packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/linkers/websocket.py ~271-274) matches only a bare `channel_layer` inside `async_to_sync(...)`. The common sync-consumer form `async_to_sync(self.channel_layer.send)(\"chat\", ...)` (and `group_send`) matches neither send regex, so it produces no send-site and no edge.\n\nRepro: fixture under the audit scratchpad (wsfix/app/) built by the docstring-staleness audit 2026-10-17 verifier; running the linker's pattern scan over it yields no send-site for that line. Also noted in the same read: `DJANGO_CONSUMER_SEND` and `DJANGO_CHANNELS_ROUTE` are compiled but never applied (already disclosed in the module docstring's \"NOT detected\" block)."  # 8d27
    fields:  # 8d27
      statement: "the websocket linker detects the Django Channels async_to_sync send idiom in sync consumers"  # 8d27
      root_cause: "DJANGO_ASYNC_SEND matches only a bare channel_layer, not self.channel_layer"  # 8d27
